<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">oasis</ansi>

The Planar Oasis is an otherworldly labyrinth of elemental
energy — a cube of shifting terrain where directions fold
back on themselves and elementals roam freely.

<ansi fg="yellow">Layout:</ansi>

  A three-dimensional maze. Moving north, south, east,
  west, up, or down wraps around — walk far enough in
  any direction and you return to where you started.

  Every room holds an elemental guardian. Somewhere in
  the maze, elite elementals and a powerful elemental
  lord wander the corridors. The lord may find you
  before you find it.

<ansi fg="yellow">Rules:</ansi>

  Death does not end your run. You may return through
  the rift and continue where you left off. Recall
  magic works here.

  Guardians do not respawn once slain — clear the cube
  methodically. The rift stays open for 30 minutes.

<ansi fg="yellow">Loot:</ansi>

  Elite elementals and the elemental lord carry planar-
  forged equipment with random properties. Oasis gear
  is stronger than Arena gear — harder to earn, but
  worth the effort. More gold invested means tougher
  guardians with better equipment.

<ansi fg="yellow">Navigation:</ansi>

  The cube wraps in all six directions including up and
  down. The entrance is your only fixed reference point.
  It is easy to become lost. Some adventurers drop items
  to mark their path.

<ansi fg="yellow">How to Enter:</ansi>

  Visit the Rift Chamber (east of Temple District).
  <ansi fg="command">ask sable oasis 200</ansi> — invest any amount over 100
  gold. Sable will tell you the exit command.

